  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through Wednesday)\nIssued at 931 PM CDT Wed Aug 5 2026\n\nThrough the long term ridging will set up both at the surface and\naloft just to our SE. This will maintain WSW flow and keep \ndewpoints in the mid 70s. Under broad ridging, highs will remain \nin the low 90s each afternoon. Temps in the 90s paired with \ndewpoints in the 70s will quickly bring heat concern back into the\nforecast. Heat indices look to flirt with triple digits each \nafternoon, yet currently remain below 105 criteria for a Heat \nAdvisory. We will continue to monitor temperature trends should an\nadvisory look more likely as the new work week draws closer.\n\nPaired with heat concerns, each afternoon will have low to medium\nchances (30-50%) for scattered showers and thunderstorms. Without\nstrong forcing, afternoon storms will pose little to no strong to\nsevere risk. Rather, lightning and heavy rainfall look to be the \nprimary threats. In weakly forced regimes like this, things can \nchange quickly especially regarding strong to severe storms. \nPlease check back for updates!",
